{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSXQZ1wGEaqiTKWizErd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a good understanding. Let me summarize my analysis:\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nAdd a POST endpoint at `/shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that confirms a shipment—moving it from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED` status—handles idempotent retries by succeeding silently on already-confirmed shipments, rejects cancelled shipments with 409, and returns 404 for missing shipments.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` — Shipment data class with shipmentId, orderId, carrier, status\n- `Shipment.kt:23-27` — ShipmentStatus enum: CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-22` — save(), findById(), existsById() methods\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-43` — POST /shipments creates shipment in CREATED status\n- `ShipmentController.kt:46-52` — GET /shipments/{shipmentId} throws ResourceNotFoundException if missing\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum with 5 existing codes\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` — converts ApiException to ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Endpoints throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler formats them automatically\n- ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409\n- All error codes defined in ErrorCode enum (immutable public API)\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath matchers\n- @BeforeEach calls repository.clear() to reset state\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Add ErrorCode for shipment state conflicts (cannot confirm CANCELLED shipment)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add tests for all scenarios (CREATED→CONFIRMED, already CONFIRMED idempotent, CANCELLED rejects, missing 404)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Wrong error codes break the API contract\n- Missing idempotent logic makes retries fail\n- Missing CANCELLED status check fails the 409 requirement\n- Adding dependencies violates constraints\n\n**Open questions:**\nThe ticket doesn't specify the ErrorCode name for the 409 case. I'll use `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` (or similar) to indicate the shipment cannot transition to CONFIRMED (covers both CANCELLED and any other invalid state). This follows the pattern of existing codes like `ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS`.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add one line to the ErrorCode enum: `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM`. This code is used when a shipment is in CANCELLED state and cannot be confirmed (409 response).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new POST endpoint method at path `/{shipmentId}/confirm`:\n   - Parameter: `@PathVariable shipmentId: String`\n   - Logic:\n     - Find the shipment by ID; if not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ...)`\n     - If status is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM, ...)`\n     - If status is CREATED, update status to CONFIRMED, save via repository, return the updated shipment with 200 OK\n     - If status is CONFIRMED, return it as-is with 200 OK (idempotent, no save needed)\n   - Return type: `Shipment` (Spring will wrap it with 200 OK via ResponseEntity<Shipment>)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and returns 200 with CONFIRMED status`\n   - `confirms an already-confirmed shipment idempotently (succeeds with no update)`\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with HTTP 409 and SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM code`\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with HTTP 404 and SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code`\n\n**Alternative I rejected:**\nI considered using a single `ValidationException` for both the CANCELLED case and any state-related conflicts, but the ticket specifically names HTTP 409 (Conflict), which maps to ConflictException in this codebase. ConflictException is for resource state conflicts, not validation violations. So ConflictException is the correct choice.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | repository.findById() | repository.save(updated) | 200 Shipment | ResponseEntity<Shipment> |\n| Already CONFIRMED | repository.findById() | (none) | 200 Shipment | ResponseEntity<Shipment> |\n| CANCELLED | repository.findById() | (none) | 409 ApiError | ConflictException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Not found | repository.findById() | (none) | 404 ApiError | ResourceNotFoundException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- **Test 1**: Create shipment → confirm it → assert 200 OK and status=CONFIRMED\n- **Test 2**: Create shipment → confirm it → confirm it again → assert 200 OK and status still CONFIRMED (idempotent)\n- **Test 3**: Manually insert CANCELLED shipment into repository → confirm it → assert 409 Conflict with error code SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n- **Test 4**: Confirm non-existent ID → assert 404 Not Found with error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1757,"cache_read_input_tokens":16942,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1757},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9546a1a2-26a9-4f02-b3d8-5e9c3b3e14e3","uuid":"7066fdc8-9d0d-4a47-a7f5-a7790ef45247","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:29:21.620Z","request_id":"req_011CfSXQYeMqBW9ZGRkmMiKi"}
