{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSXU5Hvxj1Jwq94FEAqV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! **All 17 tests pass**, including all 4 new tests I added for the confirm endpoint. The build is **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw test` returned BUILD SUCCESS with 17 tests run\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 5 original ShipmentControllerTest tests still pass (creates, rejects duplicate, returns by id, reports unknown, lists)\n3. ✅ **`POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` confirms a created shipment and persists it** — Test `confirms a created shipment and returns 200 with CONFIRMED status` verifies this; the endpoint creates a new shipment instance with CONFIRMED status via `shipment.copy(status = ShipmentStatus.CONFIRMED)` and saves it via `repository.save(confirmed)`\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Used same exception types (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException) and error code pattern (ErrorCode enum) as existing endpoints; errors are formatted by GlobalExceptionHandler\n5. ✅ **A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused** — Three test cases: `confirms an already-confirmed shipment idempotently` (returns 200 with no update), `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with HTTP 409`, `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with HTTP 404`\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — Only modified Kotlin code and tests; pom.xml unchanged\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified: ApiError.kt (added 1 error code), ShipmentController.kt (added 1 method), ShipmentControllerTest.kt (added 4 tests)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n- **ApiError.kt** — Added `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to ErrorCode enum (line 35). This is the new error code for 409 Conflict responses when trying to confirm a ca